; The uninstrumented twin: the same three sources as ../dune compiles,
; with no rewriter at all. Nothing here may name a preprocessor - that
; is the entire point of the directory, and the reason it is a
; directory: two libraries cannot claim the same module name in one.
;
; Because all three copies come from one source, no comparison in
; test_semantics.ml can drift. Adding a witness to mutsem_order.ml adds
; it to both sides at once, and a witness that exists on only one side
; is a build error rather than a silently skipped check.
;
; If a (preprocess) field ever appeared here, test_semantics.ml would not
; compile: the rewriter names its generated module after the source path,
; so an instrumented baseline grows a module the instrumented copy does
; not have and the `module type of' coercions fail. That, and not a
; count of registered files, is what makes the twin's uninstrumentedness
; a checked property rather than a comment.

(copy_files
 (files ../../../coverage_ppx/semantics/covsem_fixtures.ml))

(copy_files
 (files ../mutsem_order.ml))

(copy_files
 (files ../mutsem_boom.ml))

(library
 (name mutsem_baseline)
 (modules covsem_fixtures mutsem_order mutsem_boom))

; The plain half of the exit-code pair; ../dune runs it and diffs its
; output against the same golden the instrumented copy is diffed against.
; mutsem_exit.ml is written out here rather than copied: it differs from
; ../mutsem_exit.ml in exactly the token the pair exists to measure.

(executable
 (name mutsem_exit)
 (modules mutsem_exit)
 (libraries mutsem_baseline))
